WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.717 --> 00:00:07.162
Diego Alvarez: Morning, Marisol. Morning, Amanda. How's the week going down there?

2
00:00:08.052 --> 00:00:14.314
Marisol Vega: Hey Diego. Busy. We're in the middle of a push on the Texas pipeline, so it's calls all day.

3
00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:19.337
Amanda Pierce: Hi Diego. I'm mostly along for the finance side today.

4
00:00:19.628 --> 00:00:26.545
Diego Alvarez: Sounds good. Before we get into anything, how are the volumes looking? September felt like it came in heavy.

5
00:00:27.732 --> 00:00:36.844
Marisol Vega: It did. We tracked just under 11,400 calls across the three states last month, which is up maybe 9% over August.

6
00:00:37.215 --> 00:00:40.964
Diego Alvarez: Nice. Is that Google Ads mostly, or is Meta picking up?

7
00:00:41.611 --> 00:00:51.734
Marisol Vega: Google's still the bigger share, but Meta has been climbing since we changed the creative in July. The Spanish-language spots are doing well.

8
00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:57.410
Diego Alvarez: Good. Anything weird on the routing or the voice agent side over the weekend?

9
00:00:57.826 --> 00:01:09.457
Marisol Vega: No, it's been fine. We had a couple of agents out sick Monday, so Yolanda moved two people from the Arizona floor onto the Texas queue for the afternoon.

10
00:01:09.457 --> 00:01:10.660
Marisol Vega: That was it.

11
00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:17.425
Diego Alvarez: Okay. I saw the Salesforce outcomes are still flowing, so nothing to worry about there.

12
00:01:18.539 --> 00:01:24.711
Marisol Vega: Right. And you said you wanted to walk through something before the Q4 planning starts?

13
00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:33.874
Diego Alvarez: Yes, I sent over a calendar hold for the week of the 19th so we can prep, but I wanted to hear from you first.

14
00:01:34.411 --> 00:01:40.923
Marisol Vega: Can we do the 20th? The 19th is our district manager meetings, and nobody's free.

15
00:01:42.084 --> 00:01:45.234
Diego Alvarez: I'll move it. Now, what's on your mind?

16
00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:54.054
Marisol Vega: Let me just say it. When finance and procurement look at renewal pricing, they push back on paying separately for the add-ons.

17
00:01:54.392 --> 00:01:58.790
Diego Alvarez: Meaning the PreSense piece, the QM seats, the voice agent minutes?

18
00:01:59.208 --> 00:02:08.541
Marisol Vega: All of it. They took last year's invoice and this year's and went line by line, and the add-on lines are the ones they circled.

19
00:02:09.233 --> 00:02:12.594
Diego Alvarez: How much of that is procurement versus you and Amanda?

20
00:02:13.031 --> 00:02:22.620
Marisol Vega: It's mostly procurement. But they ask me why the seller experience we promised needs a separate line, and I don't have a good answer for them.

21
00:02:22.928 --> 00:02:30.428
Amanda Pierce: And I'll be honest with you, Diego. We've started taking calls from other vendors because of this.

22
00:02:31.474 --> 00:02:43.110
Diego Alvarez: Okay. I want to make sure I understand the shape of it before I take it anywhere. Amanda, when you say other vendors, are those exploratory conversations or something further along?

23
00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:53.484
Amanda Pierce: Exploratory. Nobody's sent us a proposal. But the add-on pricing friction at renewal is tied to whether we even get to a proposal stage with anyone.

24
00:02:53.789 --> 00:03:07.321
Diego Alvarez: That's clear. I'm not going to sit here and promise anything on the pricing structure today. What I can do is get the specifics in front of the people who own it.

25
00:03:07.551 --> 00:03:13.546
Amanda Pierce: That's all I'm asking. I need something concrete before we start building the FY27 budget in December.

26
00:03:14.752 --> 00:03:25.538
Diego Alvarez: Understood. Can you send me the two invoices, marked up the way procurement did it? That way I'm not paraphrasing when I take it back.

27
00:03:26.109 --> 00:03:28.485
Amanda Pierce: I'll get that to you by Monday.

28
00:03:29.231 --> 00:03:40.109
Marisol Vega: And Diego, on the day-to-day, everything's working. Signal AI is tagging the way it should, transcripts look right. This is a money conversation, not a product one.

29
00:03:40.673 --> 00:03:47.951
Diego Alvarez: Good to know. I'll come back to you both next week with what I hear. Thanks for being direct about it.

30
00:03:48.446 --> 00:03:50.111
Marisol Vega: Thanks, Diego. Talk soon.

31
00:03:51.568 --> 00:03:52.368
Amanda Pierce: Bye, Diego.
